figdown 0.1 bitfield
# `PRESENCE-CONDITION-EXPRESSION`: the positional PRESENCE FLAG is retired in both of its
# spellings. `optional` (…0.1, and again 0.1 after `PRESENCE-FLAG-SPELLING` reverted
# `PRESENCE-FLAG-SPELLING`) and `conditional` (0.1…0.1) are each a line error naming
# their migration; the live construct is the option key `present=`, whose
# VALUE is the presence condition. A bare flag could say only THAT a field
# was conditional — never why — so the condition had to live in the THEN-`note=`
# key, where neither the human nor the model could use it.
#
# READ THAT SENTENCE AS HISTORY, and read it that way in the golden too. When
# `PRESENCE-CONDITION-EXPRESSION` was written, `note=` on a `field` was the machine-facing tooltip key;
# `DESCRIPTION-KEY-SPELLING` renamed it `description=` in the same release, and `DRAWN-ANNOTATION-FORM`
# revived the spelling `note=` for something else entirely — the DRAWN
# annotation, which `field` refuses (case 479). So a reader arriving today
# meets "the condition had to live in note=" in the 0.1 diagnostic and
# has to translate twice: the key that sentence names is the one now spelled
# `description=`, and the `note=` that exists in the language today is not it.
# The .errors.txt golden still carries the original wording BYTE FOR BYTE
# because a golden is what the engine emits, not what a fixture wishes it
# said; re-wording it is an ENGINE edit (the `PRESENCE-CONDITION-EXPRESSION` literal in
# editor/figdown.html) and is not made here.
bitfield a "A" numbering=msb0 word=32
field "W" 16 present="C = 1"
field "X" 16 optional
field "Y" 16 conditional
field "Z" 16 present=""
